why: run 16 wrote a sentence of the same shape as the facts here, and it had to be read twice to parse, because its second verb was elided; each clause names its verb
labelled: 2026-09-29
--- code
export function declaresCurrency(posting: Posting, currency: string): boolean {
  return [posting.currency, posting.supplementalCurrencies].some((value) => value?.split(',').includes(currency));
}
--- facts
The posting format lets `currency` name only a base currency and the supplemental currencies attribute name the currency extending it.
This function therefore matches the currency against both attributes.
